games, and 3d data visualization. In some graphics

01:33:16.240 --> 01:33:24.240
and chart applications, we need a custom
colormap to achieve special visual effects.

01:33:24.240 --> 01:33:31.680
In fact, the colormap is just a table or
list of colors that are organized

01:33:31.680 --> 01:33:40.480
in some desired fashion. We can create a
custom colormap with an mx3 color matrix

01:33:40.480 --> 01:33:51.120
with each row representing RGB values. The row index
can represent the y data of a 2d chart

01:33:51.680 --> 01:34:01.680
or height of a 3d surface plot. For a given color
map matrix, the color data values can be linearly

01:34:01.680 --> 01:34:10.560
scaled to the colormap. Here shows the color
strips for the colormaps that we will create

01:34:10.560 --> 01:34:19.440
in this project. You can see that each color
map has a familiar colormap name, such as

01:34:19.440 --> 01:34:28.400
hsv, hot, cool, and jet and so on. You can
download the source code used in this project

01:34:28.400 --> 01:34:37.360
from this GitHub repository link. This specific
