surface. This function returns the normalized 3d

01:48:01.760 --> 01:48:10.320
point. For our simple 3d surface as shown here, this
surface can be formed by quadrilateral mesh grid

01:48:10.320 --> 01:48:17.200
Here is one of the quadrilateral. This, as
shown here, is a unit grid cell. This

01:48:17.200 --> 01:48:25.680
unit grid is a quadrilateral with 4 vertices
P0, p1, p2 and p3. We can divide this

01:48:25.680 --> 01:48:33.040
quadrilateral into two triangles P0-p1-
p2, this one triangle, another triangle is

01:48:33.040 --> 01:48:40.960
p2-p3 and P0 as shown here. We will
create a vertex data, normal vector data and

01:48:40.960 --> 01:48:47.920
colormap data for this quadrilateral. Now,
we can add a new function called Create_Quad.

01:48:49.200 --> 01:48:55.520
You can see here that this function takes
4 points just as shown here, point 012

01:48:56.480 --> 01:49:04.320
and 3. It takes these 4 points as its input
arguments. It also takes vertex data range y

01:49:04.320 --> 01:49:11.520
minimum and y maximum, as well as the colormap
name as its input parameters, because we

01:49:11.520 --> 01:49:16.400
want to add the colormap to the y values
for our surface. Of course you can colormap

01:49:18.000 --> 01:49:26.072
the data value in the other direction such as
x and z direction. But we usually add colormap to the y

01:49:26.072 --> 01:49:33.599
values. here we first create
the vertex position data for the six vertices

01:49:33.600 --> 01:49:39.760
This is point zero, point one,  point two.
This is the first triangle, this is second

01:49:39.760 --> 01:49:47.440
triangle: point 2, point 3, and point zero. So this
is vertices for this unit cell for these two

01:49:47.440 --> 01:49:55.120
triangles. Next, we define the normal vector for
this quadrilateral. We already discussed how to

01:49:55.120 --> 01:50:02.720
obtain the normal vector for this quadrilateral
in the previous project. It is simply equal to

01:50:02.720 --> 01:50:10.480
the cross product of these two diagonal lines of
this quadrilateral. Here we introduce these two

01:50:10.480 --> 01:50:18.160
lines: first is p2-p0, p two p zero,
we call the CA, another line is  p3 and

01:50:18.160 --> 01:50:25.680
p1, p three P one, we call it DB. Then, we get
the cross product, we call CP, these two lines,

01:50:25.680 --> 01:50:33.600
then we normalize this CP cross product, we get
the normal vector for this quadrilateral. So, all

01:50:33.600 --> 01:50:41.440
the vertices on this quadrilateral have the same
normal vector. Next, we add the colormap data

01:50:41.440 --> 01:50:49.840
